                Native whey is filtered directly from milk rather than collected as a by-product of cheesemaking, so it skips the cheese process. Ascent has long marketed native whey, and its current whey label includes native whey protein isolate within an isolate blend. The research showing native whey beats good conventional whey for results is limited.
